# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo and on checkout.
#
# Without this, contributors on Windows (where `core.autocrlf=true` is
# the default git install setting) get CRLF in their working tree and
# Biome's formatter reports every file as a diff. The check is platform-
# correct but practically unrunnable. Pinning LF here makes `pnpm lint`
# pass identically across Linux / macOS / Windows.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary; `eol=lf` forces LF on
# checkout for everything classified as text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary asset types — never normalize, never diff as text. These would
# corrupt if git tried to translate line endings.
*.glb       binary
*.gltf      binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.webp      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.icns      binary
*.blend     binary
*.blend1    binary
*.ogg       binary
*.mp3       binary
*.wav       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.zip       binary
*.tar       binary
*.gz        binary
*.exe       binary
*.dll       binary
*.dylib     binary
*.so        binary

# Shell scripts must stay LF even if a future contributor's git is
# weird. Belt + suspenders given `* text=auto eol=lf` above.
*.sh        text eol=lf

# --- Compiled/exported runtime assets → Cloudflare R2 (NOT git/LFS) -----
#
# Track / bike / prop GLBs, hero & thumb JPGs, texture-atlas PNGs, and the
# opus soundtrack are served from Cloudflare R2 (bucket `hoverbike-content`
# at https://hoverbike-content.mattscott.dev), and are gitignored under
# public/assets/ + public/audio/. The app fetches them via
# VITE_ASSET_BASE_URL — see src/engine/asset-url.ts and docs/asset-storage.md.
#
# They were moved off git-LFS to stop Vercel from re-pulling ~160 MB of LFS
# objects on every deploy (the GitHub LFS-bandwidth blowup). No LFS filter
# rules remain — `pnpm assets:pull` / `assets:push` sync them with R2.
